rable garment is carried out able willingness to join the Territorial Force, in very soft thick satin of a particularly be- MADGE. • coming shade of mole grey; the accompany- ing cloth skirt being, of course, of exactly the same shade. The satin is draped in fichu style over each shoulder, and is drawn down t..) the. front in .charming artistic f01d.3,</p>
        <p>where it is met by a very high corselet-waist- band of Singularly handsome design. This waistband is carried ..cut in the atin, but is adorned in front with a very handsome orna- ment 'composed of thick silk cord and. em- broidery. Over the tops of the sleeves the fiehu-like drapery develops into a sort •of little ovensleeve, which is edged with hand- some silk fringe: Between the draped fronts comes a dainty vet of tucked Breton net, and the long, close-fitting, tucked sleeves -aro carried out in the same material. HAIR ORNAMENTS.</p>
        <p>The question of hair ornaments is one that is just now calling for a good deal of atten- tion. So far, writes Mrs. Hugh Adams; the dainty erinine bands, terminating in a 10r.a.; black osprey or plume, have not "caught on" to any great extent in London, however popular they may be in Paris... One of the prettiest novelties in this direction is an . old paste • slide worn under the back dressing, through which is threaded a wide band of soft satin ribbon destined to be threaded ihrough the hair c r tied in a Gneuze band round the bead. 'Wreaths and silver leaves and bands of big jot- beads terminating in an upstanding osprey are also favourite modcs of the moment. A POLI TICAL APPEAL.</p>
        <p>The Women's Social and Political Union which last year rlised £2,000 by a "self- denial week," have asked their members throughout the Country to make special con- tributions during Lie week beginning Satur- day, February 27th.</p>
