      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-01-30_WidnesExaminer_art0016" n="art0016">
        <head>LONGER AGO THAN YESTERDAY.</head>
        <p>LONGER AGO THAN YESTERDAY.</p>
        <p>Yesterday is not long ago, but nearly three and a half years is. To have been cured long ago and to have been well; ever since, surely means a permanent cure. Here is what a Newton-le-Willows woman has to say about it.</p>
        <p>Airs. E. Cooke, 45, Golborne Dale-road, Newton-le— Willows, writes :—" Dear sirs : For some time I was. subject to acute pains in my back and stomach, and although I tried different treatments, I could get no relief,' "One day I happened to read about Doan's pills, and I sent for some to fry. I have been a great deal better since using this medicine, and my back has been much easier, lithe pains return, I shall take some more of Doan's pills. (Signed) Mrs. Cooke." Speaking to one of our representatives, three and a half years later, Mrs. Cooke said :—"I still keep quite well. I was very bad when I first used Doan's pills. I had been fifteen weeks under medical treatment. I could not straighten my back, it was so bad, and I had severe headaches and nasty giddiness also : I had palpitation of the heart as well. I often think I would, not have got tetter had it not been for Doan's pills,. for although I took other medicines, I was growing weaker all the time. I am indeed grateful for my cure." • If you are suffering from Backache. Urinary Disorders, Rheumatism, Dropsy, Gravel, Neuralgia, or any other kidney trouble, Doan's Pills will cure you; they will cure your kidneys, the cause of your illness, If you neglect your kidneys you must suffer from painful and dangerous disease. The kidneys are the keys of health; keep them well and you will be well. Above all things remember that delay is dangerous. Doan's Backache Kidney Pills are two shillings and ninepence per box (six boxes for thirteen shillings and ninepence). Of all chemists and stores, or post free, direct from Foster-McClellan Co., 8, Wells-street,. Oxford-street, London, W.—Mrs. Cooke was cured by Dean's; be sure that you " DOAN'S."</p>
