        <head>EDUNTITA COMMITrEE.</head>
        <p>EDUNTITA COMMITrEE.</p>
        <p>THE INCREASES IN TRADERS' SALARIES.</p>
        <p>The monthly meeting of the Warrington Education Committee was held at the Town 11311 oa Monday evening, Councillor J. Fulton-Smith .presiding. Thera were also present :—Mr. 11. Roberts (deputy-chairman), Aldermen Bennett, EL lison, S:nethurst, Councillors Raton, Dickenson, Dr. Joseph, Lord, Pemberton an:! Wilkinson, Rev. .1. Yonge, Miss Williams, Niessri. C. Sawkins Burgesq T. P. Br idshaw. R. r. Fairctough, A. J. Jolley, B. Plinston, C. H. IJusworth, .1. Upson, G. Walker, J. Moore Murray (director), John Fairhurst (treasurer).</p>
