      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-01-30_WidnesExaminer_art0063" n="art0063">
        <head>VICTIMS OF THE WEATHER.</head>
        <p>VICTIMS OF THE WEATHER.</p>
        <p>Peps Indispensable for Throat &amp; Lungs.</p>
        <p>Sudden weather changes are .prolific of coughs, colds, sore throat, bronchitis, pleurisy, and pneumonia, especially, at this season when frost, stir, sleet, rain, fog and biting winds take their turn with humid and muggy days. There is no better safeguard under the prevailing weather conditions than a box of Peps. A few little Peps crushed in the mouth, or. merely dissolved on the tongue, provide a timely tonic and antiseptic for the throat, lungs, and chest. Delicate tissues which are most susceptible to chill and disease, such as the mucous membrane lining the bronchial tubes (tissues which cannot be reached by ordinary medicine), are bathed in the rich fumes emitted from the dissolving Peps tablet. Inflammation is allayed, the injury caused by incessant coughing, wheezing and sneezing, is repaired, and all chest troubles are positively arrested in the , first stages. If a few Peps are taken before venturing out on a bleak day, or when one is thinly clad for theatre or dance, they will give adequate protection against chill. You can always rely on Peps, for they are free from opium, morphia, cocaine, chloral, laudanum, or any other narcotics or sedatives. Even tl.e children can take them at any time and iu any quantity, with perfect safety. Be sure that you get the genuine, which has the registered name - Peps on every box. You will then know you have the one natural and reliable cure for .coughs, colds, bronchitis, chills, sore throat, asthma, laryngitis, hoarseness, Croup, whooping cough, influenza, and other throat and chest complaints. Of rh chemists at is. 1 d. or 2s. 9d., or post fee from the Peps Company, Carlton Hill, I.eeds.</p>
