        <p>-+- SELL HIM FOR NELSON.</p>
        <p>A man was passing through Farringdon Strezt, when he accid,utally knocked a little statue of Wellington off a stall, and broke off one of his arms. The owner asked the man if ,be were going to pay for it. The man asked: "'What have I done? " Knocked his arm off," said the owacr. "Well, knock his eye out, aril- sell him for Nelson," said the man.</p>
        <p>--t Paddy ha 1 a pig which he regularly crammed one day and, starved the next When asked why he did so, he repl:ed : " Och, sure, and isn't it I that like to have my bacon with a strake of fat and a strake o' lane aqually, one fter Calker ?"</p>
