        <p>ASSOCIATION FOOTBALL. -- WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT LEAGUE. FIRST DiVISION.</p>
        <p>For ag'st P. W. L. D. G. G. P. Lymm _ 13 11 2 0 52 11 92</p>
        <p>Earlestown St. John's 12 10 2 0 55 11 20 Burtonwood</p>
        <p>W'gton Albions Res. 8 5 2 1 23 15 11 Latchford _ __ __ _</p>
        <p>flylands' Orford Whitecross Burtonwood Wesley H 2 8 1 17 24 5 Halton SECOND DIVISION. Mown St. John's Res. 8 8 0 0 25 1 19 Burtonwood Reserve Newton Amateurs 7 3 3 1 10 8 7 The!wall United Lymm Reserve Whitecross Reserve Walker's Frodsham Brotherhood 6 , 0 4 2 4 18 2 . .</p>
        <p>- ...... Halton Res. and Rylands Res. withdrawn. Record expunged. Matches for January 30th. Ist Division :—Lymm v. Warrington Albions. Whitecross v. Burtonwood. _ _</p>
        <p>24---DiVisiOn-i.-11'h-elw-ali United v. Whitecross Reserve. Burtonwood Reserve v. Walker's. Result of Matches January 23rd. Ist Division :—Lymm 3, Burtonwood 0.</p>
        <p>Albions 5, WbiteCross WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT ELEMENTARY SCHOOLS' LEAGUE. RESULTS TO DATE.</p>
        <p>—Goals—</p>
        <p>P. W. D. L. For Agst. Pts Parochial Ileathside l4 ... 11 ... 2 ... 1 ... 42 ... 7 ... 24 Ar pl ey-street 13 ... 8 ... 2 ... 3 ... 27 ... 30 ... 18 Wycliffe l2 ... 8 ... 0 ... 4 ... 21 ... 13 ... 16 St. James' l2 ... 5... 2 5... 29... 18 ... 12 St. Barnabas' lO ... 6 ... 0 ... 4 ... 21 ... 19 ... 12 Silver street ll ... 4 ... 1 ... 6 ... 21 ... 24 ... 9 St. Mary's lO ... 3 ... 3 ... 4 ... 15 ... 22 ... 9 Beamont Hamilton at l2 ... 2 ... 4 ... 6 ... 19 ... 29 ... 8 Trinity Christ Church 14 ... 1 ... 3 ... 10 ... 15 ... 73 ... 5 St. Alban's 12... 0 ... 2 ... 10 ... 1 ... 43 ... 2 The Parochial boys continued their vicorious career and will soon have reached the century. Their record is remarkable, as may be seen by a glance at the League table. In tho two matches played since Christmas they have scored 25 goals, whilst their own citadel has not fallen once. lk weak Arpley-street team was routed to the tune of 12-0, and the following Saturday Christ Church was out-classed 13-0. In the latter game the Parochial boys did nothing but shoot,and large as the score was it would have been much larger but for the good goal- keeping. The match was simply one boy versus eleven. The Now Year start disastrously for fleatbside, Wycliffe defeating them 2-1 after a poor game. rhe losers somewhat redeemed them by defeating Hamilton- street 3-1 in their succeeding match. They now take second place in the table. The Wycliffe combination must be looked upon as most inconsistent. After beating the strong Heathside team by 2-1 they lose to a very weak Arpley-street team by the same score reversed. Trinity did a smart performance when they defeated St. James's by 3-1.</p>
        <p>FOOTBALL FIXTURES AND RESULTS.</p>
        <p>(NORTHERS UNION LEGI.7E.)</p>
